        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70379,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Testis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70380,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/140\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Teratoma, prepubertal-type</em> and <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/142\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Yolk sac tumour, prepubertal-type</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70381,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours occur very rarely in the testis. Therefore, their real incidence is unknown, but case studies suggest that pure prepubertal-type YSTs are at least 10&nbsp;times as frequent as prepubertal-type mixed tumours {14634440; 15247758; 23707551}. Mixed tumours have also been reported in adults, with 2&nbsp;well-supported cases, 1&nbsp;in a patient with Down syndrome {25427839}. See also <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/140\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Teratoma, prepubertal-type</em> and <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/142\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Yolk sac tumour, prepubertal-type</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70382,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/140\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Teratoma, prepubertal-type</em> and <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/142\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Yolk sac tumour, prepubertal-type</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70383,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The current hypothesis is that YST develops in a teratoma. In sacrococcygeal teratomas, the presence of immature elements is assumed to be associated with an increased risk of progression towards YST {16410129; 9737245}. Although progression in an early, small, immature teratoma may result in a pure YST by overgrowth, progression in a fully developed teratoma may manifest as a mixed tumour. See also <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/140\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Teratoma, prepubertal-type</em> and <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/142\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Yolk sac tumour, prepubertal-type</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70384,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases have the same macroscopic appearance as prepubertal-type teratoma, because the YST foci are usually small.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70385,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>YST foci in teratomas are usually small and associated with immature elements, making them easy to overlook on microscopic examination {9737245; 15613854}. Immunohistochemical staining for AFP or SALL4 can help highlight YST components, although weak to moderate expression can also be demonstrated in immature teratomatous elements {19428066; 24525512; 32222813}. The tumours are not associated with germ cell neoplasia in&nbsp;situ.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70386,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70387,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours lack 12p abnormalities. See also <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/140\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Teratoma, prepubertal-type</em> and <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/142\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Yolk sac tumour, prepubertal-type</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70388,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a combination of teratoma and YST elements in the absence of germ cell neoplasia in&nbsp;situ.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> immunohistochemical staining for YST (e.g. AFP); absence of 12p abnormalities.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70389,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/142\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Yolk sac tumour, prepubertal-type</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70390,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In the absence of metastasis and with adequate AFP normalization after surgery, adjuvant therapy is not required and the patient should continue to be followed up. In the rare case of systemic disease, further management is based on YST therapy.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-21T11:57:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]